  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="guide-tips-title">
    <p class="panel-step">03 · TIPS</p><h2 id="guide-tips-title">To get what you want</h2>
    <div class="guide-cards">
      <article><h3>Edit an image</h3><p>Attach the image, then write what changes <strong>and</strong> what must stay. “Only change the red pot to cobalt blue. Keep the characters, the table and the lighting.” works better than “make the pot blue”.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep a composition</h3><p>A seed finds settings again, not an image. To start again from a creation you like, attach it as a reference from the library.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Exact names and text</h3><p>For a diagram or a poster, prepare an illustration with empty slots. Then add the labels with “Exact, editable text”: you can correct them, move them and download a PNG, an SVG or the JSON project.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep the brief’s intentions</h3><p>Add the required subjects, relations and important words in “Constraints to keep in the brief”. They stay word for word when Hermes rewrites the description. Then check that they are present in the result.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Show the composition</h3><p>Place named zones in “Composition sketch”, then attach the guide as a reference. It takes one of the two available slots. Save its JSON project to change the placement later.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Review an edit</h3><p>“Compare with the parent original” shows both archives side by side, or with a sliding divider when their dimensions match. Note the kept elements and the differences in your checklist, then save the JSON review.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Keep the rest of the image</h3><p>With a parent and an edit of the same dimensions, choose the rectangles to take back in “Keep the parent outside the chosen zones”. The composition checks the kept pixels before the PNG and the receipt are downloaded.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Two references</h3><p>Give each one a role: “image 2 is only a material sample; apply it to the orange robot in image 1”. Without a role, the model may repaint the wrong element.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Quick try, then polished render</h3><p>Look for the idea with the recipe that has the fewest steps. When the brief is right, redo it with the polished recipe, attaching the try if you want to keep its composition.</p></article>
      <article><h3>Logo or sticker</h3><p>Asking for a transparent background has not given a usable result in our trials. Ask for a plain background instead and cut it out afterwards.</p></article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="guide-section" aria-labelledby="guide-blocked-title">
    <p class="panel-step">04 · WHEN IT GETS STUCK</p><h2 id="guide-blocked-title">What the messages mean</h2>
    <dl class="guide-messages">
      <div><dt>“Image queued”</dt><dd>The request is recorded and waits for its slot. Only one image uses the card at a time. Check the same receipt; there is no need to repeat the request.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>“GPU busy”</dt><dd>The check at launch found another use of the card. Check the result of this operation before deciding on a new try.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>“The image PC is unavailable or the required model is missing”</dt><dd>The keeper does not answer, or the requested recipe is not installed. The request is refused before it enters the queue.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>“Uncertain state”</dt><dd>AgentX no longer knows whether the image was computed, for example after a restart. Use “Check and recover”: it finds the result without ever restarting the computation.</dd></div>
      <div><dt>“Its archiving must be resumed”</dt><dd>The image exists but could not be kept. The retry stores the original without recomputing it.</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <p class="image-help">An accepted image may start once within the 15 minutes following its request. If the slot expires, it is cancelled. The result stays viewable and an uncertain computation is never restarted automatically.</p>
  </section>
</main>
